1
00:06:20,869 --> 00:06:26,869
Separated by war. Tested by battle. Bound by friendship.

2
00:12:41,739 --> 00:12:47,739
War Horse is a war, history, adventure film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:19:02,608 --> 00:19:08,608
On the brink of the First World War, Albert's beloved horse
Joey is sold to the Cavalry by his father.

4
00:25:23,478 --> 00:25:29,478
Against the backdrop of the Great War, Joey begins an odyssey full of danger,
joy, and sorrow, and he transforms everyone he meets along the way.

5
00:31:44,347 --> 00:31:50,347
Meanwhile, Albert, unable to forget his equine friend, searches the
battlefields of France to find Joey and bring him home.

6
00:38:05,217 --> 00:38:11,217
Albert Narracott, played by Jeremy Irvine.

7
00:44:26,086 --> 00:44:32,086
Ted Narracott, played by Peter Mullan.

8
00:50:46,956 --> 00:50:52,956
Rose Narracott, played by Emily Watson.

9
00:57:07,826 --> 00:57:13,826
Grandfather, played by Niels Arestrup.

10
01:03:28,695 --> 01:03:34,695
Lyons, played by David Thewlis.

11
01:09:49,565 --> 01:09:55,565
Capt. James Nicholls, played by Tom Hiddleston.

12
01:16:10,434 --> 01:16:16,434
War Horse is a 2011 war drama film directed and produced by Steven
Spielberg, from a screenplay written by Lee Hall and Richard Curtis.

13
01:22:31,304 --> 01:22:37,304
It is based on Michael Morpurgo's 1982 novel and its 2007 stage adaptation.

14
01:28:52,173 --> 01:28:58,173
The film features an ensemble cast that includes Peter Mullan, Emily Watson, Niels Arestrup, Jeremy
Irvine (in his feature film debut), David Thewlis, Tom Hiddleston and Benedict Cumberbatch.

15
01:35:13,043 --> 01:35:19,043
Set before and during World War I, its plot follows Joey, a bay Irish Hunter horse raised by English teenager Albert as he is bought by
the British Army, leading him to encounter various people throughout Europe, in the midst of the war and its tragedies.

16
01:41:33,913 --> 01:41:39,913
DreamWorks Pictures acquired the film rights to the novel in December
2009, and Spielberg was announced to direct in May 2010.

17
01:47:54,782 --> 01:48:00,782
Having directed several films set during World War II, it was
his first to tackle the events of World War I.

18
01:54:15,652 --> 01:54:21,652
Shot in England over 63 days, the production used 5,800 extras and 300 horses.

19
02:00:36,521 --> 02:00:42,521
Several longtime Spielberg collaborators—including producer Kathleen Kennedy, cinematographer Janusz Kamiński,
editor Michael Kahn, production designer Rick Carter and composer John Williams—worked on the film.

20
02:06:57,391 --> 02:07:03,391
Produced by DreamWorks and distributed worldwide by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures through the Touchstone Pictures label, War
Horse became a box-office success (earning $177 million on a $70 million budget) and was met with positive reviews.

21
02:13:18,260 --> 02:13:24,260
The film was named one of the ten best films of 2011 by the American Film Institute and the National Board of Review,
and was nominated for six Academy Awards (including Best Picture), two Golden Globes and five BAFTAs.

22
02:19:39,130 --> 02:19:45,130
The film explores themes of world war i, horse, farm life, execution, trapped.
